WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.629
Red carpets, private jets, exotic locations
— the life of an actor may seem pretty plush.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:09.680
But don't forget that being an actor requires
work, and it often means running into some

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.440
pretty uncomfortable situations.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:15.600
When things go too far and a star declines
to do a scene, fans can't help but speculate

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.540
as to what kind of drama went down on set.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.440
Here's a look at some movie scenes that actors
refused to film.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.200
Body double

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:28.080
Isla Fisher's breakthrough role as "stage-5
clinger" Gloria Cleary in 2005's Wedding Crashers

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.700
catapulted her to fame — and earned her
a reputation as a comedic force.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:36.320
The film was a huge hit at the box office,
thanks in part to raunchy R-rated gags.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:40.880
But as far as Fisher was concerned, unclothed
scenes were an absolute dealbreaker.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.040
In an interview with Entertainment Weekly,
she elaborated on just how many scenes she

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.200
skipped…and how many stand-ins her shooting
contract stipulated.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.100
She said:

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.000
"I had a hand double for the under-the-table
scene.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.960
I had a breast double for the boob-in-the-face
and I had a butt double.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:57.540
My argument was, if you see a character's
breast, she's no longer funny.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:59.320
I lost that argument with the producers."

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:00.780
Too Furious

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:05.780
The Fast and the Furious franchise is a juggernaut,
but production on the eighth installment,

00:01:05.789 --> 00:01:10.259
The Fate of The Furious, was less than full-speed
ahead thanks to the competing egos of two

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:13.340
of the franchise's biggest stars — Dwayne
Johnson and Vin Diesel.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:17.799
In fact, it was ultimately revealed that the
beef was so bad, the two totally refused to

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:18.540
film together.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:23.040
It all started in 2016, when Johnson went
on a social media rant during filming.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.030
In a since deleted Instagram post, he wrote
in part:

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:30.240
"Some [men] conduct themselves as stand up
men and true professionals, while others don't.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.560
The ones that don't are too chicken s— to
do anything about it anyway."

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.880
TMZ reported that the day after, Johnson and
Diesel had a hush-hush meeting — which pretty

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:41.520
much confirmed that Diesel was the subject
of Johnson's social media vent session.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:46.580
Sources reported that things were so uncomfortable
on set that it was "impossible to shoot scenes."

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:51.640
In a 2018 interview with Rolling Stone, Johnson
himself confirmed that they didn't film any

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:55.409
scenes together, and his scenes with Diesel
in The Fate of The Furious were the product

00:01:55.409 --> 00:01:56.820
of clever post-production work

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:58.580
"It ain't too late to stop this."

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.120
The end for Emma

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:12.080
Emma Watson has demonstrated serious range
in a variety of roles since breaking through

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:16.470
as a child actor in Harry Potter… but none
of it prepared her for her uncomfortable cameo

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:17.480
in This Is the End.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:21.680
The dark comedy was pretty much exactly what
you'd expect from Seth Rogen and his writing

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.840
partner Evan Goldberg, whose over-the-top
sensibilities were established with Superbad.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:26.820
"Here let me see it."

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:27.320
"It's real, it's heavy."

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.020
"Ahhh!

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:30.520
Come on, guys!"

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:32.400
"Bang bang!"

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:37.020
Like the rest of the all-star cast, Watson
played an exaggerated version of herself — but

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:40.860
she didn't exactly feel welcome in the boys'
club atmosphere during filming.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:45.250
According to an extra, Watson walked off the
set over a scene featuring Channing Tatum

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:47.760
in a surprise cameo, doing the full-on Magic
Mike.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.360
"Channing introduce yourself."

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.280
"What's up, guys.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:52.060
You cool?"

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.060
"It's Channing Tatum!"

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:55.280
"It's Channing Tatum!"

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.020
"What the f---!"

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:59.460
PopFocal picked up the since-deleted blog
post, which alleged,

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:03.620
"Channing decided to do some of his breakdancing
in front of her but alas he was in nothing

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:04.300
but a thong…

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.640
Emma storms off set…

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.220
So we wrapped the night 5 minutes later."

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:11.599
James Franco seemed to confirm the story in
conversation with Interview magazine.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:12.320
He explained:

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.280
"So a funny thing happened on this movie I'm
doing.

00:03:14.549 --> 00:03:18.180
The movie is a comedy, but it's kind of an
outrageous one, and this actress — I won't

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:21.800
say who, but she had a smaller role in the
film — walked off the movie in the middle

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:22.300
of a scene."

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:26.900
Watson has never commented on her alleged
exit, although she later indicated that she

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:28.020
enjoyed her time on the film.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:33.260
"How could I miss out on the chance to work
with some of the best, the most impressive

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:36.940
lineup of the best comedians in the world
right now."

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:38.620
Absentee Blade

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:43.840
The Blade trilogy was Marvel's first three-quel,
but the final installment, Blade: Trinity,

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:47.060
didn't exactly wow audiences when it premiered
in 2004.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:51.920
Panned by critics as being shallow and scattered,
it left fans disappointed — especially after

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:55.580
Snipes filed a lawsuit against the production
company after the film's release.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:06.280
Eight years after the film came out, cast
member Patton Oswalt shed some light on what

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:10.080
went down — namely that Snipes allegedly
refused to film most of his scenes.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:11.280
Oswalt told the A.V.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:11.780
Club,

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:15.019
"He wouldn't come out of his trailer […] he
only [came to the set] for close-ups.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.680
Everything else was done by his stand-in.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.280
I only did one scene with him."

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:22.820
Oswalt also revealed that Snipes had big beef
with writer-director David Goyer, stemming

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:25.780
from an argument during a night out in Vancouver
while filming.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.380
As the feud continued, things only got more
ridiculous.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:32.220
"After a while he resorted to giving people,
communicating with post-its.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:37.220
He would give one to the director, each one
he would sign 'Blade.'"

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:38.740
Off Pitch

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:43.780
Anna Kendrick found international superstardom
in Pitch Perfect as Beca, The Bellas' rebellious

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:48.040
soprano — and it sounds like her real-life
personality isn't far from the tough-talking

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:49.720
undergrad she played on the big screen.

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:53.560
Kendrick spoke out about putting her foot
down on a potential storyline that had Beca

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:57.130
getting romantically involved with a record
executive who was trying to get the Bellas'

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.120
master of the mash-up to sign with his label.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:00.980
She told Harper's Bazaar UK:

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:05.780
"Originally the music executive was supposed
to be my romantic interest but I said no to

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:08.420
that, because I thought that would be kind
of f—ing problematic."

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:12.140
In the same interview, Kendrick revealed that
she pushed back on producers who asked the

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:14.860
Bellas to step into more revealing wardrobes,
saying:

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:15.660
"It's funny.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:18.970
Whenever we do the wardrobe fittings I feel
like we get notes from the top saying they

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:21.040
should be tighter [...] and show more skin.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:23.280
And I'm like, that's not why people are coming
to see the movie."

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:24.980
Kissing pains

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:30.320
Kirk Cameron's strict Christian faith means
that he considers even the smallest onscreen

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:34.950
romantic gesture to be risqué — which is
why he told producers of the 2008 faith-based

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:38.080
family drama Fireproof that he wouldn't be
kissing his co-star.

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:42.320
As Cameron claimed during an appearance on
the Today Show, it wasn't just the kiss — he

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:47.440
clashed with producers over several storylines
he felt were immoral, mainly that his firefighter

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:49.860
character spends much of the film contemplating
divorce.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:54.040
That commitment to marriage meant that Cameron
refused to film the big kiss scene the way

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:54.640
it was written.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:59.190
So the film crew changed up the scene, utilizing
low lighting and tight angles to put Cameron's

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:01.780
own wife in the shot, dressed up in the female
lead's costume.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:02.900
Awww.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.560
And they say romance is dead.

